# 11. OFFLINE-FIRST FUNCTIONALITY

This is a critical requirement.

The app must work without internet.

Use Room database as the local source of gameplay data.

Store locally:
- Player profile
- Selected character
- World and stage data
- Approved question bank
- Mission definitions
- Player progress
- XP
- Coins
- Medals
- Local achievements
- Game session history
- Pending synchronization operations

When offline:
- The app must launch normally.
- The player must be able to continue the story.
- The map must be accessible.
- Downloaded missions must work.
- Mini-games must function.
- Progress must be saved locally.
- No blocking internet error should appear.

When online:
- Authenticate or refresh the player session.
- Synchronize local progress.
- Download approved content updates.
- Upload pending gameplay results.
- Receive updated announcements and settings.
- Refresh online rankings.

Use WorkManager for reliable background synchronization.

Implement retry logic and clear sync status indicators.

Avoid duplicate reward transactions.

Use unique operation IDs and idempotent synchronization.

IMPORTANT SECURITY RULE:

Offline results must be marked as pending verification.

Do not allow the Android client to directly modify authoritative online XP, coins, medals or leaderboard scores.

When the device reconnects, send the pending results to a trusted backend validation process.

Only validated results may enter the official online leaderboard.

If the backend cannot verify an offline result, preserve the local history and show an appropriate pending or rejected status without deleting the player's progress.

Implement conflict handling for synchronization.

Never silently overwrite newer server data with older local data.

